# WS5-02/04 (library lifecycle, failure paths), A1200/KS3.1 under FS-UAE
# (54x-fs-uae.sh case 542). Sources: spec/appendix-stdlib.md and
# stdlib/std.amiga.workbench.clo (savePublicScreen "Returns false for a null/unknown
# screen or an unwritable path"); intuition.library autodocs (LockPubScreen returns
# NULL for an unknown name); exec.library (a library call needs an opened base).
# The shim defines IntuitionBase itself (NULL until a screen or window opens), so
# libstubs' auto-open object is not linked (link map, sieve.clo.map in WS4).
# Expected: "calling", "saved false", rc 0, END.
# Contrast 542c (a screen is opened first): the same lines.
# Detector: a crash leaves no END line within the timeout.
expect: script
--- output
before vertb N port 0 card 1
calling
saved false
rc 0
after vertb N port 0 card 1
END
